---
import BaseLayout from "../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../shared/config/config";
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle="Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Start Here — Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  description="A practical orientation for people who want to stop problematic pornography use: how to use this platform, what recovery involves, and honest expectations."
  canonical="/start/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Start Here", url: "/start/" }]}
>
  <h1>Start Here</h1>
  <p>If you are trying to stop or reduce problematic pornography use, this page explains
  how to approach it and how to use this platform.</p>

  <h2>Step 1: Understand what you are dealing with</h2>
  <p>Problematic pornography use (PPU) means porn use that feels out of control and causes
  distress or problems in your life. Many people describe cycles of urges, use, and regret.
  Understanding the cycle is the first practical step. See <a href="/recovery/">Recovery</a>.</p>

  <h2>Step 2: Read how others actually recovered</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/experiences/">Experiences</a> section contains de-identified, structured
  reports from community members: what triggered them, what they tried, what happened.
  These are personal reports — not scientific proof — but they show what real recovery
  attempts look like.</p>

  <h2>Step 3: Learn your own triggers</h2>
  <p>Community reports repeatedly describe specific situations that precede urges:
  late-night boredom, stress, loneliness, being alone with a phone. Recognizing your own
  triggers is consistently reported as a turning point. See <a href="/triggers/">Triggers</a>.</p>

  <h2>Step 4: Try structured strategies</h2>
  <p>People report many practical strategies — exercise, environment changes, blockers,
  accountability, therapy. What works varies by person. See
  <a href="/strategies/">Recovery Strategies</a>.</p>

  <h2>Step 5: Know what the evidence says</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/research/">Research &amp; Evidence</a> section separates what people
  report from what science has established — and clearly marks what remains debated.</p>

  <h2>Honest expectations</h2>
  <p>Recovery is rarely linear. Many community members describe setbacks as part of the
  process — not as failure. This platform never promises fixed timelines. See the
  <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> page to understand how content here is produced
  and labeled.</p>

  <p class="note">If pornography use is causing you significant distress, or you feel
  depressed, anxious, or unable to cope, professional support may be appropriate. This
  platform provides educational information, not a substitute for care.</p>
</BaseLayout>
